cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Thermoelectric Discovery Engine: a physics-informed transfer-learning
  calibration layer for SnSe/SnS thermoelectric transport prediction
message: >-
  If you use this software, or the calibrated models it ships, please cite it
  using the metadata below. Please also cite the upstream KRICT work listed
  under "references", which this software is derived from.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sadashivaiah
    given-names: Nischal
    affiliation: >-
      College of Intelligent Computing, Chang Gung University, Taoyuan, Taiwan
repository-code: 'https://github.com/NischalRaj16/thermoelectric-discovery-engine'
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end framework for predicting, screening and calibrating the
  thermoelectric figure of merit ZT of SnSe- and SnS-based chalcogenides from
  100 to 1000 K. A frozen ensemble of gradient-boosted models supplies a
  first-principles transport prior from multi-valley DFT descriptors; four
  residual correction models, validated out-of-fold with GroupKFold
  partitioned on formula, map that prior onto measured experimental transport.
  The engine adds explicit crystallographic-direction encoding for the
  anisotropic Pnma/Cmcm lattice, physical bounding of the effective-mass
  tensor, a self-consistency audit against ZT = S^2 sigma T / kappa, a
  domain-validity guard that flags extrapolation, and Materials Project convex
  hull screening for synthesisability.
keywords:
  - thermoelectrics
  - machine learning
  - transfer learning
  - SnSe
  - SnS
  - figure of merit
  - materials informatics
  - density functional theory
  - XGBoost
